A||||40||87FieroGTx||Why don't we spend mega $$$ like the import guys?||||1||
Z||000000||87FieroGTx||11-25-2001||10:46 PM|||| Why don't we(Fiero owners) spend mega $$$ like the import guys?<P> I went out to an import car hangout Friday and most of them have spent over 30k on there cars and some spend as much as 80k<P> The most I've seen spent on a Fiero is the Great Blue Choptop (25K??) but most of us have under 10k into our cars, Hell.. most of us have under 2k into them.<P><BR> I have a few thoughts on this but I want to hear your views.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jsears8||11-25-2001||10:51 PM||||I would if I could afford it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I want to do an LS1 swap into my 88 Fiero.  Leave it all stock looking on the outside except for a nice set of wheels.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Justin<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jsears8" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/jsears8</A> <BR>98 Trans Am<BR>88 Fiero 2.5<p>[This message has been edited by Jsears8 (edited 11-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||11-25-2001||10:52 PM||||'cause we're not in high school and we don't have daddy's check book to work with?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg">     <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||8
Z||000003||California Kid||11-25-2001||11:08 PM||||Tough question to answer.....you'll get a lot of feedback on this one.  Basically I think everyone one has some goal in mind regarding what they want their car to be, and how much they want to put into it.<P>My investment is under the tops you mentioned, but the car consistently pulls 1st and 2nd place trophies in nearly all shows I've entered (14 to date). I like it the way it is, probably only make some small dollar changes in the future (like flush lamps, etc). In my case I don't feel the need to throw a lot more money at it, have better places I'd rather put it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/californiakidsig_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroMaster88||11-25-2001||11:10 PM||||Because we dont need to to look good!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000005||recluse||11-25-2001||11:17 PM||||These high school import kids spend all this money because they think its making their car "cool" and we all know that if you have a "cool car" then you ARE cool.  And its all a trend, its the newest craze since Korn and blonde hair dye.  This is from what I've seen.  I can understand if you are racing your car in competitions of some kind, but just to drive up and down the street, and up and down some more... its stupid.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Stage-2GT||11-25-2001||11:26 PM||||Basically it has to do with brains and or the lack there of. I have seen several specials on TV regarding this phenomenon. These guys are in hock up to there eyeballs. Eventually, most of them will loose there precious rides to bankruptcy because they don't have the means to support their habits. These people are losers from the word go. First off they believe that it will make them popular and second they have no real way to afford it. It all winds up as a burden on the tax payers. In fact, we, Fiero owners, are doing our part to keep America solvent. We bought American and we spend within our budgets. Just my .02]<P>S2GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||firstfiero||11-25-2001||11:34 PM||||     We already start out with a good looking car. The civic guys have to spend alot of money to get their little family to car to look sporty and be somewhat fast. I've raced some seriously modded hondas with my v6 and beat them. We don't need a body to kit to make our car look good...they do. We already have the big rear spoiler.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Theirs cash saved. And we already have a quick car to start out with. Unless ya got a v-tech you have some serious money spending to get you some horsies under the hood. And we already have the exhaust! We don't need to spend alot of money to make our cars have a good deep throaty exhaust ... we already got it. Hell they spend all that money on exhaust and they still sound like they have a trunk full of bee's!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> So ya see were already way ahead of the game!<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||11-25-2001||11:36 PM||||Well, I have roughly 10-15k into my car over the last 7 years.  Compared to today's value, I overpaid for the car by almost double (but then it was a "deal" at the time). Also most of the money has gone into necessary restorations (Paint, Motor, Tranny, Exhaust)- all of which were required for operation.  I just chose to spend slightly more to have them "better/faster" than stock.<P>As to why I haven't spent $30k...?  Hmmm let's see- House (mortgage payment & associated bills), general taxes, living expenses, Wife (not expensive... just an associated cost of living), and more!  I have more priorities in my life than my car (although for the amount of time I spend on the forum you wouldn't think so...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  Anyway, I don't need to spend that kind of cash to make my car look nice and/or go fast!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Last Dodo||11-25-2001||11:41 PM||||I have seen both sides of the fence here and it seems to me that we don't have quite the backing that the rice boys (and girls) have.  They have umpteen thousand parts available for their cars and they have to pretty much buy them.  We have to pretty much build or modify existing parts to do the same thing.  Bolt-on really doesn't apply to a Fiero.  Each piece we have to buy is more expensive than a comparable piece on a Honda for example so many of us can't afford it.  I don't blame the manufacturers of the products for this.  They are doing all they can to keep the prices at a minimum because they love these cars as we do, but everything costs money.  If you can build 1000 copies of something they will be cheaper than if you build 100.  <P>Ask a Honda owner sometime the last time he had to personally modify the bolt spacing on his Civic to get more wheel options.  I'll bet you'll get a strange look.  We spend less because most of us upgrade our cars the old fashioned way with wrenches and drills.  <P>We are also using mostly (for lack of a better term) junkyard parts and a used part is usually cheaper than a new one.<P>I have not ben on this forum long, but I have owned my Fiero for a long time and I have been keeping tabs on what is happening in the Fiero world almost as long.  Everyone who has ever posted here and anyone who will are the people who keep us alive.  I'd rather Modify mine any day.<P>This is strictly opinion, but thanks for letting me vent.  And remember, you asked.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BlackStang95||11-26-2001||12:51 AM||||Import parts (even stock replacements) cost more in general than domestic ones.  But I think the main thing is most ricers don't know how to do a damn thing themselves and pay a place to do it (which they often put big decals on advertising, basically admitting they didnt do it themselves).  You guys know what I'm talking about?||||reg||1
Z||000011||The Fieromaster||11-26-2001||01:36 AM||||Cause most of us dont live with mommy and daddy and IF we do they dont buy EVERYTHING under the sun FOR US!!  Hell i HAVE rice and i cant afford to make it RICEYER!<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||11-26-2001||01:44 AM||||Actually, We don't need to sink $30K into our Fiero's to make them fast. We are starting with an inexpensive platform.<BR>People like Archie, Chris West, Bob Steiger, Chris Moore, Ed Parks, and all the others, can give us PLENTY of power. With $30K I'd have one of the fastest Fiero's PLUS 2 different daily drivers, and still have money left over!!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Shaun41178||11-26-2001||01:48 AM||||There are fiero owners out there that have spent quite a bit on their cars.<P>However I would say the majority of Fiero owners on this board don't spend as much on their Fieros cause they are cheapos.  Come on admit it.  You see a lot of import guys spending thousands of dollars for turbo kits and supercharger kits.  All you hear from Fiero folks is how expensive a $3k turbo kit is and how they are going to do it for less without even knowing how a turbo works.<P>Or how you hear, make a supercharger kit and we will buy one.  So RSM does make one.  How many people have ponied up to that kit so far?  I would say about a handfull.  How many on this board?  Maybe one.  Lots of talkers in the Fiero community but little doers.  How many import enthusisasts have stepped up?  Thousands.<P>I think the younger guys on this board are serious about modding up their Fiero and are working to buy the mods to do it.  It just takes some time working for $6 an hour.<P>For the older folks on here,(35+) the Fiero is their midlife crisis car cause they can't afford a Vette but want it to perform like one for no invested money cause "I don't want to invest $3k into an engine upgrade when I only paid $800 for the whole car" excuse.  <P>I am sure many won't agree with me but I could care less cause I am not a talker, I am a doer.||||reg||9
Z||000014||fierospeeder||11-26-2001||02:02 AM||||just call the ricers terroists because they are trying to ruin the US's economic system by buying foreign.<P><BR>on speedvision, they had a ricer show.  All i can say its just a waste of time and money.  When my g/f and i see a lowrider truck, we just say "what a waste"<P>"honey, can you go to home depot and pick me up some 40lb bags of topsoil"  I cant honey, my truck will bottom out.<P>------------------<BR>Fiero Technician<P>74 Vw Beetle<BR>83 Honda Nighthawk 550<BR>84 Pontiac Fiero<BR>87 Ford Thunderbird Turbo<P>Selling a car is like giving your own kid for adoption.||||reg||1
Z||000015||DKOV||11-26-2001||02:04 AM||||Really... what can we do to a Fiero to make it any better anyway?<P>Motor swap, handling kit, big brakes... The best things about the car are already there so everything else we do is more about identity than "coolness".<P>The Fiero is too cool to begin with.  Why mess with that?  Bigger, Faster, Stronger... That's a different motivation!<P>We, as Fiero owners, are less interested in sitting around looking at the "pretties" on our cars than completely blowing away a unsuspecting 'Vette  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Stealth is more fun anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000016||artherd||11-26-2001||02:09 AM||||1) Because the cars don't totally suck from the factory (at least in performance.)<P>2) Because we're whiney, cheapass bums!<P>Honestly!<P>We've got Fieros because we can't afford a used Ferrari (and a few extra $k for the deserved maintinence thereof.)<P>We think brake upgrades should cost $100.  We thing *3grand* for a FULL TURBO KIT is too expensive!!!<P>We think three grand for brakes that WILL NOT KILL US AND THOSE WE LOVE is 'too high a price to pay'<P>WE WON'T PONY UP $500 BLOODY DOLLARS FOR A SET OF FULLY COATED HEADERS PLUS Y-PIPE!!!<P>We like to talk about how fast our 84 4-cyl automatics are going to be after $23 worth of junkyard parts, and we pretend the 4500rpm limit of a 4.9caddy v8 dosen't suck (it does.)<P>We also work hard for our money, and somehow think we can get away with driving a mid-engine exotic sports car on a sub-GM-FWD-grocery-getter budget.   Just because we paid $2k for the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>(PS: no offence to any 2M4 auto owners.<BR>There's always V8 Archie and a 5-speed conversion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000017||fieroX||11-26-2001||03:17 AM||||I live with my mommy and she hasnt paid for any part of my fiero.  She did buy me a new carburetor for my firebird for my birthday, but that doesnt count. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Mach10||11-26-2001||03:20 AM||||Cos I'm BROKE damnit! You wanna MAKE somethin' of that?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000019||The Fieromaster||11-26-2001||03:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroX:<BR><B>I live with my mommy and she hasnt paid for any part of my fiero.  She did buy me a new carburetor for my firebird for my birthday, but that doesnt count. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Im not talkin about EVERYONE who lives with mommy.. Im talkin about the little bitches around here with their COBRAS and they are JUNIORS in school and dont work... and how they have all these mods on them!  The kids who dont do dick but have parents pay for it all BUT then they trash it cause they dont respect it cause its not their money payin for it!! THATS who im talkin bout!<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Last Dodo||11-26-2001||03:51 AM||||I gotta admit, if I had 30 g's to spend on anything I would still have only about 3 g's left after I got myself outta debt.  But I would still use that on the car.<P>  I agree with many of you, priorities first. Food before Fiero. <BR> <BR>  Why don't we spend, maybe cheap, maybe strapped for cash, maybe frugal, maybe more inclined to modify instead of replace?  I'm sure everyone has a different reason.<P>  Me, Uncle Sugar don't pay worth a crap and I have to do this piece by piece and maintain a family at the same time.  My wife would kill me if I dropped that kind of money.<p>[This message has been edited by Last Dodo (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||RedOktober||11-26-2001||05:06 AM||||the people that are willing to spend more than 30K for their upgrades usually dont hang out here. <P>Here is a car a friend built, very little Fiero left, only trans, susp, and steering column, and VIN. It looks great, but most peple dont call em Fieros anymore. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/512c_1.gif"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/512b_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Fformula88||11-26-2001||10:19 AM||||I am sure there are some big Fiero spenders out there.<P>Most import owners don't spend that much either.  The percentage of imports expensively modified and Fiero's with tons of money in them may be about the same too.  remember, there was only 375K Fiero's made (approximate)... period.  There are many more imports made aper year that are desireable to tuners.  Therefore, there will be a lot more highly modded imports.<P>All in all, it doesn't make sense to me anyway.  If I had 30K-80K to drop in a car, I can think of a lot of nice cars I would want before buying an import and doing all kinds of stuff to it.  You really have to be into modding a car to sink that kind of cash into it.  To each his own.||||reg||1
Z||000023||pHoOl||11-26-2001||10:41 AM||||I am living with mommy and daddy, and the car is in his name because i didn't pay for it....  YET.  Some people would say that i'm spoiled because my dad bought the car for me to use.  However... the only reason that he did was because i have promised to pay him back for any and all expenses of it after i am out of college and making money.  I look at it more of like a loan.  Some people up here at school try to tell me that i'm the same as the spoiled kids who get Saleens for their fifteenth birthday so that they can learn to drive on them.  <P>I think there is a big difference between a 50 thousand dollar car, and a two thousand dollar car.  And yes... someday i will throw some dollars at it, but not when i'm in school and broke as hell.  <BR>I rolled past one of those guys in my city that i went to high school with and he had a riced jetta.  Rolled up and laughed.  He tailed me around the city until he could get next to me, then gave me a dirty pout, and revved his bumble bees up.  Didn't want to waste my time.<P>The kids in my city with rice burners are either paying for it off daddy's check, or they're dealing.  Not sure which, but neither would suprise me.||||reg||1
Z||000024||88CoupeV6||11-26-2001||10:45 AM||||Because it doesn't take 30K to make our cars cool, but I've never seen many cool imports either  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||12
Z||000025||ChopTop||11-26-2001||01:24 PM||||Sometimes it’s more about perception than it is about reality.  I’d like to see a price break down between hardware and labor prices.  I’m going to assume anyone who says they have 80k in their car did very little of the wrenching themselves, and very little of the original car remains.  Labor can easily double to triple your end cost.  Also these guys are probably including the initial price of their cars which could run anywhere from 12K on up (depending on the model and options).  Bartering is also popular with these guys (just as it is with domestic enthusiasts), you give me a retail 5 or 10K paint job, I’ll build you a retail 5 or 10K motor.  But when someone asks how much did your paint/motor cost, they are going to include the retail price.  <BR>Your question may have more to do with statistics than our willingness to spend big bucks.  From the Fiero car shows I’ve been to lately their seems to be a growing willingness to outspending each other.  If you really want to know how much a car is worth, wait until they go to sell it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||dennis_6||11-26-2001||01:31 PM||||30K on a fiero?  Even if I had the money I couldn't do it.  With the same money I could buy me all of the following:<BR>1992 GTA<BR>1990 Silverado 4x4<BR>1987 Fiero GT with LS1 installed by Archie<BR>1979 Trans AM<P>I could never justify 30K in one car.||||reg||1
Z||000027||SLAMMED87GT||11-26-2001||01:44 PM||||I think a big part of this is the fact that we started out with a unique car. There is nothing  else like the Fiero really. Therefore we don't need to spend so much to make it look "cool" or "different." We can spend plenty if we want to customize though.<P>The Ricers on the otherhand are starting off with a car that is generally basic and there are many of them. Some of which are actually family cars (i.e. 4-door Accords, Civics). If they don't put money into the car for a body kit or wheels to make it look different, then they will just have a basic Honda Civic.<P>Although there are some that spend money on actually making their cars faster (Fiero and Imports), there are many that just want it to look fast.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>It's not only an import thing, but that is the "fad" these days and really, a change in the automotive industry. They are changing some of the imports to cater to the young demograhic by means of different looks and a good job of marketing.<P>SOOOOOO.......spend money where you want to, and if you are the one that earned the money your are spending, be proud!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig_1.jpg"> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto540 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||6
Z||000028||Red2m4||11-26-2001||01:45 PM||||If I was going to spend 80k dollars on a car, it would be a Ligenfelter Twin Turbo Corvette.  If I was going to spend 80k dollars on a Civic, I would expect my friends and fellow forum members to give me shock thereapy.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChopTop:<BR><B>If you really want to know how much a car is worth, wait until they go to sell it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ChopTop has a point...but, <P>If you really want to know what a car is worth, see how it does at the track.  I've seen some really nice $20-30k hot rods that would blow the doors off a moded Honda/Toyota, and look better doing it. <P>I didnt mean to buy a fiero, but i got a deal on a low-mileage car, it just kind of grew on me.  I once agreed to switch shifts with a coworker who's 2nd job was at a detailing shop.  I got a $150 dollar detailing job for free.  The car looked brand new, got more looks than a PT cruiser.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000029||GT Bastard||11-26-2001||01:53 PM||||Keep in mind.... They've already financed at least $20,000 on a 5 year loan.  Next step, apply for a few credit cards with a 1,000-2,000 limit.  Voila! They're rich!  At least for a while.  That's really how it works around here. Otherwise the car was simply given to them by rich parents for graduation.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/icare.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000030||GTFiero1||11-26-2001||03:43 PM||||Because Fieros came awsome from the factory<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<P>you gotta keep on keepin on...||||reg||1
Z||000031||Pheagey||11-26-2001||03:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Cos I'm BROKE damnit! You wanna MAKE somethin' of that?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>DITTO! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed;<BR>Have you seen my website yet?<BR>Http://www.LithiumEffects/pheageysfeiro<BR>"The car formaly know as, and has now reverted back to being known as, Pheagey's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000032||Spektrum-87GT||11-26-2001||05:11 PM||||well, i live at home with my parents, but i've paid for every little thing(and big thing) in my car!<P>reasons i dont put 30k into my car? well thats simple, 30k is a down payment on a nice house. I also cant seem to convince myself that it would cost 4 months worth of work to make my car go faster... i'm content with the acceleration  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> 1200 for brakes is a little expensive too... i'll just be a little more careful when i drive. to each his own though! personally, i think the fiero(gt) only lacks cool wheels and lowering springs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>so are fiero owners cheap? i dont believe so... practical yes, cheap no.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/spektrum_87gt/" TARGET=_blank>87 Fiero GT</A><BR>1991 Jeep Cherokee<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.com/bspracklin1/sig2.jpg">   <BR>AIM:<FONT COLOR="red">S</FONT><FONT COLOR="purple">p</FONT><FONT COLOR="blue">e</FONT><FONT COLOR="cyan">k</FONT><FONT COLOR="green">t</FONT><FONT COLOR="yellow">r</FONT><FONT COLOR="orange">u</FONT><FONT COLOR="red">m</FONT><FONT COLOR="purple">1</FONT><FONT COLOR="blue">1</FONT><FONT COLOR="cyan">7</FONT><BR>And no! i'm not gay dangit!||||reg||1
Z||000033||LT1 Chop Top||11-26-2001||06:28 PM||||Anyone can make payments! <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lt1choptopsig_1.gif"> ||||reg||12
