Z||000037||donny||11-26-2001||11:08 PM||||I agree with banditbalz that does say it all.The reason I have my 86 gt is because I like it stock.No other reason really.The only 2 other cars that I would actually drive below 80 grand would be an 88-91 mustang gt or a 1993 rx-7.I would not trade my car for either of them but I do plan on adding them to my collection.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000038||DKOV||11-27-2001||02:26 AM||||I realized today that spending 30K on a Fiero IS possible... but why?<P>Looks great as is.  Performs as is.  Is FUN as is...<P>More HP and handling is always a plus that most of us can't resist but it is ALWAYS practical  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>It's not like we smack GREEDY stickers all over our cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyway, in retrospect, I think I have dropped around $16,000 on my Fiero...  Heck, the brakes alone were $2500, the motor swap another $3800, wheels/tires were $1500, new suspension package $2700...  Geeze, I better stop thinking!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyway, it IS different than the rice-o-matics... I'm not sure how yet, but it IS.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -<P>||||reg||1
